# Next.js frontend

- **App Router** + **TypeScript**; Server Components by default, Client Components only when needed (`"use client"`)
- Colocate route UI under `app/`; shared UI in `components/`; API clients/helpers in `lib/`
- Prefer server-side data fetching for authenticated/booking data; avoid exposing secrets to the client

## Patterns

- Typed props and API responses; no `any` unless justified
- Keep forms and interactive booking flows as Client Components; presentational pages as Server Components
- Call the Python backend via a thin typed client — don't duplicate business logic in the frontend

```tsx
// ✅ Server Component fetches; client only for interaction
export default async function BookingPage({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {
  const booking = await getBooking(params.id);
  return <BookingDetail booking={booking} />;
}
```

## Style

- Follow existing design system if present; otherwise keep UI minimal and consistent
- Avoid overbuilding dashboards or card grids unless the product requires them
